63],[123706351,"Tigerjagd",1907,0,1,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,64],[124413256,"Village Landscape with Figures",1902,0,1,null,0,"4/4f/Rousseau_-_Village_Landscape_with_Figures%2C_ca._1895-1910%2C_67.24.13.jpg/330px-Rousseau_-_Village_Landscape_with_Figures%2C_ca._1895-1910%2C_67.24.13.jpg",0,0,1,0,15],[126075958,"Paysage, le pont",null,0,1,null,0,"8/80/Henri_Rousseau_-_Paysage%2C_le_pont.jpg/330px-Henri_Rousseau_-_Paysage%2C_le_pont.jpg",0,0,1,0,65],[133467619,"United Family",1896,0,1,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,66],[133814888,"Landscape with Tiger and Hunters",1907,0,1,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,67]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"548141":["The Dream is a large oil-on-canvas painting created by Henri Rousseau in 1910, one of more than 25 Rousseau paintings with a jungle theme. His last completed work, it was first exhibited at the Salon des Indépendants from 18 March to 1 May 1910, a few months before his death on 2 September 1910.","The Dream (Rousseau)"],"960447":["Tiger in a Tropical Storm or Surprised! is an 1891 oil-on-canvas painting by Henri Rousseau. It was the first of the jungle paintings for which the artist is chiefly known.","Tiger in a Tropical Storm"],"1219263":["The Sleeping Gypsy is an 1897 oil on canvas painting by the French Naïve artist Henri Rousseau (1844–1910). It is a fantastical depiction of a lion musing over a sleeping woman on a moonlit night.","The Sleeping Gypsy"],"3207251":["The Snake Charmer is a 1907 oil-on-canvas painting by French Naïve artist Henri Rousseau (1844–1910).","The Snake Charmer (Rousseau)"],"3319184":["Myself, Portrait-Landscape is an oil on canvas self-portrait by Henri Rousseau, from 1890. It is held in the National Gallery Prague.","Myself, Portrait-Landscape"],"3399446":["Portrait of Mr. X is a painting by the French artist Henri Rousseau. Rendered in simplified forms, it depicts a half-length figure of a man with a cat set against a landscape background.","Portrait of Mr. X (Pierre Loti)"],"4952174":["Boy On The Rocks is a painting by French artist Henri Rousseau. It is an oil on canvas and was created sometime between 1895 and 1897.","Boy on the Rocks"],"7741023":["The Hungry Lion Throws Itself on the Antelope is a large oil-on-canvas painting created by Henri Rousseau in 1905.","The Hungry Lion Throws Itself on the Antelope"],"19912313":["The Repast of the Lion is an early 20th century painting by French Post-Impressionist Henri Rousseau. Done in oil on canvas, the work depicts a feeding lion in a jungle setting.","The Repast of the Lion"],"19912798":["The Banks of the Bièvre near Bicêtre is an oil-on-canvas painting executed c. 1908–09 by French artist Henri Rousseau. It depicts the working-class community of Bicêtre on the outskirts of southern Paris.","The Banks of the Bièvre near Bicêtre"],"59511250":["The Muse Inspiring the Poet is a 1909 oil-on-canvas painting by the French artist Henri Rousseau, forming a double portrait of Marie Laurencin and Guillaume Apollinaire. Owned for a time by Paul Rosenberg, it is now in the Kunstmuseum Basel.","The Muse Inspiring the Poet"]}}